WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.000
Hell no on Kavanaugh!

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:06.220
Some people are very upset over

00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:07.520
Donald Trump's pick

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:08.880
for the Supreme Court.

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:10.800
He is a dangerous man!

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:13.120
Are you ready

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:14.560
for a fight?

00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:16.300
What are they so upset about?

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:19.960
What's at stake is freedom for LGBTQ Americans,

00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:21.980
for equal rights,

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:23.300
for civil rights!

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:24.660
People are freaking out.

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:26.080
They are freaking out because

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:28.300
they don't understand those top areas,

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:30.180
whether it's abortion or gay rights,

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:32.460
or Citizens United that people on the left

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:33.960
tend to be concerned about.

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:35.640
There's really not gonna be a change.

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:37.420
That's because the court, especially

00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:39.090
Chief Justice Roberts

00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:40.600
respects precedent,

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:42.200
especially when people have come to

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:44.620
depend on previous decisions.

00:00:46.820 --> 00:00:49.080
After a quarter-million gay marriages

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:52.060
and 45 years of legal abortions,

00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:55.080
the court's unlikely to reverse itself on those issues.

00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:56.548
I will nominate

00:00:56.548 --> 00:00:58.700
Judge Brett Kavanaugh.

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:01.400
But if Kavanaugh replaces Kennedy,

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:03.420
there will be changes.

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:04.860
Individual freedom.

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:06.740
What does Kavanaugh mean for that?

00:01:06.740 --> 00:01:08.720
He's great there, probably better than Kennedy.

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:10.280
Retiring Justice Kennedy

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:12.820
sometimes ruled against individual liberty,

00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:14.340
like when he said it was okay

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:17.100
for a Connecticut town to grab Suzette

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:19.500
Kelo's property and little pink house

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:22.680
because the developer who might pay more in taxes

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:23.940
wanted her land.

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:25.880
Kennedy voted for the bad guys.

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:29.040
He voted to take away the property from the people.

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:30.990
Kavanaugh could very well be the fifth

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:32.820
vote to overturn Kelo.

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:35.120
Trump's nominee has got to go! Hey hey!

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:38.340
One major area that people might be upset about is

00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:39.720
affirmative action.

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:41.860
We won't stand for Donald Trump's attempt

00:01:41.860 --> 00:01:45.320
to use the Supreme Court as a weapon

00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:47.720
against all of our progress.

00:01:47.720 --> 00:01:49.520
Kavanaugh could provide the

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:52.640
fifth vote to overturn that 40 year-old

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:55.700
experiment with using racial preferences

00:01:55.700 --> 00:01:57.380
to promote some kind of nebulous

00:01:57.380 --> 00:01:58.100
diversity.

00:01:58.100 --> 00:01:59.620
Lawsuit against Harvard University

00:01:59.620 --> 00:02:01.020
for discriminating against

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:02.420
Asian-American applicants.

00:02:02.420 --> 00:02:05.180
That case against Harvard's racial preferences may

00:02:05.180 --> 00:02:07.070
reach the Supreme Court soon and the

00:02:07.070 --> 00:02:09.180
court may end affirmative action.

00:02:09.180 --> 00:02:11.180
The court with Kavanaugh on board may also

00:02:11.180 --> 00:02:13.200
toss out some gun restrictions.

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:15.170
He has written one of the leading lower

00:02:15.170 --> 00:02:17.040
court opinion expanding the scope of the

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:19.380
individual right for armed self-defense.

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:20.394
He's not a gun nut.

00:02:20.394 --> 00:02:21.517
He's a constitutionalist.

00:02:21.520 --> 00:02:22.900
Kavanaugh has a history of

00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:25.120
reining in government regulators.

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:26.700
All these alphabet agencies

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:28.960
that increasingly intrude in people's lives,

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:31.080
he has written at length that the

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:33.060
government keeps doing things that it

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:34.660
doesn't have the power to do.

00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:36.940
The Constitution's separation of powers

00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:39.000
protects individual liberty.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:41.460
At his nomination announcement at the White House,

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:43.520
he talked about how the separation

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:46.080
of powers is there to protect liberty.

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:48.170
That's fantastic. I think Libertarians

00:02:48.170 --> 00:02:50.600
will like the push-back on government excess.

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:52.540
But Kavanaugh does side with

00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:54.900
government on one form of excess.

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:56.780
The government was collecting all of our

00:02:56.780 --> 00:02:58.400
metadata, all of our phone records.

00:02:58.420 --> 00:03:00.760
Kavanaugh ruled that he was just fine with it.

00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:03.380
He said that the NSA is justified

00:03:03.380 --> 00:03:05.560
in collecting metadata on

00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:06.893
Americans as part of the--

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:08.460
He volunteered to write that.

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:09.980
He was enthusiastic that

00:03:09.980 --> 00:03:11.780
this serves a critically important

00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:14.520
special need - preventing terrorist attacks.

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:16.579
But the government says we're

00:03:16.580 --> 00:03:19.000
aware of no instance where the

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:20.980
program discovered an attack.

00:03:20.980 --> 00:03:22.120
That's his worst case.

00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:23.800
Now it's unclear how that

00:03:23.810 --> 00:03:26.180
extends beyond the national security

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:27.760
surveillance area.

00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:29.020
He has a lot of good opinions

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:30.920
on police needing a warrant or

00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:33.260
laws being drawn so broadly

00:03:33.260 --> 00:03:35.820
that prosecutors are convicting people who

00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:36.735
are not guilty.

00:03:36.740 --> 00:03:37.760
Clearly he defers to the

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:39.520
government on national security grounds,

00:03:39.520 --> 00:03:42.380
but most judges and justices do anyway.

00:03:42.380 --> 00:03:44.720
At least on other forms of regulation,

00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:46.740
Kavanaugh has a strong record

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:48.660
of not deferring to government.

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:52.540
We have a moral obligation to act on climate.

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:54.920
As a judge in DC, Kavanaugh voted to

00:03:54.920 --> 00:03:57.240
strike down some environmental rules.

00:03:57.240 --> 00:03:59.739
Some EPA regulations where the staff

00:03:59.740 --> 00:04:02.040
just said, we're gonna do this?

00:04:02.040 --> 00:04:02.780
That's right.

00:04:02.780 --> 00:04:04.280
I mean, I like the idea of clean

00:04:04.280 --> 00:04:05.520
air and clean water.

00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:08.660
There are federal laws that protect that,

00:04:08.660 --> 00:04:11.440
but in the last decade, the EPA has taken a

00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:12.540
lot of liberties.

00:04:12.540 --> 00:04:13.800
But it's their job.

00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:15.469
Clean the air, clean the water.

00:04:15.469 --> 00:04:17.980
EPA does not get a free-floating power under the

00:04:17.980 --> 00:04:20.000
Constitution or otherwise to do what

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:21.100
they think is best.

00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:22.820
It's Congress' job to say, you know our

00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:24.160
air isn't clean enough.

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:26.480
Here's how you should be doing your job, EPA.

00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:28.400
Why is it better for Congress to do it?

00:04:28.460 --> 00:04:29.500
Congress is elected,

00:04:29.500 --> 00:04:30.960
and if we don't like what it's doing,

00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:31.900
we can fire it.

00:04:31.900 --> 00:04:33.740
That's the way the checks and balances work

00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:36.080
And that's why it's so important that courts

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:38.660
hold the bureaucrats feet to the fire.

00:04:38.660 --> 00:04:40.420
Hey hey, ho ho,

00:04:40.420 --> 00:04:42.600
Kavanaugh has got to go!

00:04:42.600 --> 00:04:43.940
The Libertarians should definitely be happy

00:04:43.940 --> 00:04:44.700
with Kavanaugh.

00:04:44.700 --> 00:04:46.140
He's not going to agree with us

00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:47.920
all the time certainly,

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:50.040
but no justices or judges do.

00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:52.680
The fact that we're looking around the edges to see

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:55.200
what sorts of things we can disagree on

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:58.060
shows how far we've moved in 10 or 20 or

00:04:58.060 --> 00:04:59.040
30 years.

00:04:59.040 --> 00:04:59.880
Right.

00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:01.440
At least now people and

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:04.120
judges talk about limiting government

00:05:04.120 --> 00:05:06.580
and how regulation's out of control.

00:05:06.580 --> 00:05:07.700
That's new

00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:10.540
compared to the last 10, 20, or 30 years.

